Commercial Redistribution

Commercial redistribution of the Software in its original or
Minimally Modified form is prohibited.

Commercial redistribution of a Modified Product is permitted,
including distribution without source code, provided that the
Modified Product contains Substantial Functional Modifications.

"Substantial Functional Modifications" means modifications that add
material new functionality or capabilities that were not present in
the Software.

The following changes alone do NOT constitute Substantial Functional
Modifications:

(a) changing the project name, product name, logo, icon, branding,
    copyright notice, or other identifying information;

(b) changing colors, themes, text, layout, or other primarily
    cosmetic user-interface elements;

(c) repackaging, recompiling, containerizing, bundling, or changing
    installation or deployment methods;

(d) changing configuration files or default settings;

(e) dependency updates, minor bug fixes, localization, translations,
    documentation changes, or similar maintenance changes;

(f) any combination of the above.

A Modified Product may be distributed commercially under proprietary
terms and its modifications are not required to be made available in
source-code form.

However, the copyright notice and this license notice for portions
derived from the Software must be preserved.
